ork to stabilize the rest  of the building they face another  looming threat  a tropical storm has formed in the  atlantic and could track into south  florida  early next week pharah jackson proskow  in surfside florida thank you jackson  former u.s president donald trump's  company and its longtime  finance chief have been charged in what  prosecutors called a  sweeping and audacious tax fraud scheme  the indictment accuses the company of a  long-running conspiracy to help  executives including  chief financial officer alan weiselberg  evade  taxes on perks and bonuses while at the  same time decreasing the company's  own tax obligations donald trump says  his company's actions were  standard practice and in no way a crime  trump has not been charged at this stage  of the investigation  still ahead a new statue in honor of  princess diana  brings a royal rift back into the  spotlight  oh a huge crash that massive crash at  the tour de france on saturday is  apparently causing too much commotion  for the races organizers  they're withdrawing the lawsuit against  the spectator  who took down dozens of cyclists with  her cardboard sign  french police are still investigating  and the 30 year old french woman could  face up to two years in jail  race organizers say they're dropping the  complaint because the story  has been blown out of proportion  prince william and harry put differences  aside during the unveiling of a statue  in honor of their mother  on what would have been princess diana's  60th birthday  as crystal gomencing reports the statue  is a lasting tribute  to reflect diana's courage and  compassion  that defined the people's princess  their mother so often a unifying force  once again had the royal brothers within  arm's reach  as they honored the woman they and their  country love  so dearly for many  this is how they choose to remember  diana princess of wales  a doting mother a fashion icon and a  champion of the sick  and underprivileged a joint statement  was shared and posted on social media by  prince william and prince harry saying  every day we wish she were still with us  and our hope is that this statue will be  seen  forever as a symbol of her life and her  legacy  but the brothers relationship and their  highly publicized feud  could end up being all that's talked  about in the days ahead  i hope that we can keep the focus there  but there's no doubt that there will be  some talk about the drama some talk  about why megan's not there  why kate's not there you know if the  brothers stand next to each other don't  stand next to each other if they speak  if they don't speak  backs were turned while the princes  greeted guests and their mother siblings  but they also stood together chatted  smiled  and paid tribute to the woman they  dearly wish  was still in their lives the sculptor  said we wanted to capture her warmth and  humanity  while showcasing the impact she has had  across  generations everyone can now pay  tribute to the people's princess crystal  gomanson global news  london next the 11 year old boy nova  scotia who's walking for six days to  send  one powerful message  an eleven-year-old boy in nova scotia  began his long journey today  in memory of victims and survivors of  residential schools  landon tony will travel more than a  hundred kilometers  by foot landon is being accompanied by  his mom  and cousin and he's encouraging others  to join along  as ross lord reports he hopes his walk  will serve as an inspiration  at age 11 landon tony already has the  strength of his convictions  landon is walking for six days 157  kilometers  from his house in valley nova scotia to  the annapolis valley first nation  it's his way of honoring victims and  survivors of residential schools  it doesn't feel right like that there  was  kids my age that were dying from  older people like they got  whipped and stuff when they were bad and  they couldn't go home and if they tried  to they would either get killed or  punished landon is channeling his anger  into positive action i just want people  to feel better about themselves and  i just want people to know what's going  on  and that it wasn't too long ago too  like that could have been me in one of  those graves  his mother marsha mcclellan is helping  coordinate landon's journey of awareness  creating an online fundraiser and  joining the walk to make sure  her son stays safe he's proud to be who  he is  and he wants others to be proud of who  they are  and he wants people  to learn the truth  a painful truth for landon and his  migmaw ancestors  his great-grandmother was a survivor of  the residential school in nearby  shubenacity  where a search for remains that started  last year continues  his cousin keaton is also joining the  walk it shows people how  strong we are and how much we are gonna  we will  will stand up for our for our rights and  for our heritage  for this journey landon is stepping into  new territory  i do sports but i i never went for a  long walk in my life  but embarking on this challenge will be  worthwhile he says  if it helps others ross lord global news  landon you give us hope for the future  and that is global national for this  thursday i'm farin asser  thank you so much for spending part of  your canada day with us  we leave you tonight with orange  tributes from across the country  orange letters spell out every child  matters on a busy street in vancouver bc  to honor the survivors and victims of  residential schools  and the tower at the canadian museum of  human rights is shining orange in  winnipeg  wishing you peace this canada day  however you choose to commemorate  you
 

